WEBVTT

01:33.583 --> 01:35.833
We're the only two survivors
from our company.

01:38.625 --> 01:39.666
We have won,

01:40.916 --> 01:42.416
but this is the price of war.

01:44.208 --> 01:46.458
They paid a far greater price than we did.

01:47.500 --> 01:50.583
We killed more than
1,000 Pakistani soldiers.

01:52.291 --> 01:53.375
It's not about them.

01:55.041 --> 01:56.500
It's about our soldiers.

01:57.583 --> 01:59.083
That's why I'm here.

02:02.208 --> 02:04.125
This was neither the first war
nor the last.

02:06.083 --> 02:09.208
But the wars to come
will not end like this.

02:19.791 --> 02:21.125
A secret program.

02:24.208 --> 02:27.333
To prepare the next generation
of Indian soldiers.

02:28.708 --> 02:32.541
Soldiers who will rewrite the rules
of warfare.

02:35.458 --> 02:37.375
I have the trial permission.

02:39.875 --> 02:42.583
But to make sure the program stays
permanent, I need you.

02:43.916 --> 02:44.958
Why me?

02:46.666 --> 02:49.375
Because you know
the price of war, Guru <i>ji.</i>

03:18.791 --> 03:20.583
India's most important offshore oilfield,

03:21.791 --> 03:22.791
Mumbai High,

03:24.166 --> 03:25.375
is in great danger.

03:32.166 --> 03:35.125
<i>Terrorists have attacked Mumbai High
via a sea route.</i>

03:35.708 --> 03:37.958
<i>Twenty-eight ONGC workers are being
held hostage.</i>

03:39.250 --> 03:41.791
<i>If we try to save them,</i>

03:42.166 --> 03:45.500
<i>they've threatened to blow up
the oil rig.</i>

03:46.375 --> 03:49.208
The terrorists have the hostages
and the first-mover advantage.

03:49.750 --> 03:50.958
How will you defeat them?

03:51.583 --> 03:52.541
Come in, Charlie One.

03:53.208 --> 03:55.083
This is Colonel Fateh Singh Lakhawat.

03:56.541 --> 03:58.207
<i>Team, proceed to target.</i>

03:58.208 --> 04:01.332
Risking such an important mission
with a new team?

04:01.333 --> 04:03.791
Not a risk. Guts.

04:05.625 --> 04:06.583
No guts…

04:07.958 --> 04:08.958
no glory.

04:11.083 --> 04:14.332
How can they breathe without
oxygen cylinders?

04:14.333 --> 04:17.833
My soldiers can hold their breath
underwater for seven to nine minutes

04:18.291 --> 04:20.208
<i>without reducing their swimming speed.</i>

04:28.666 --> 04:30.749
<i>Alpha One. Fourteen targets in all, sir.</i>

04:30.750 --> 04:33.665
Seven on deck, four in the control room,

04:33.666 --> 04:35.750
and three on the lower level
with the hostages.

04:36.166 --> 04:39.916
They aren't wearing night vision glasses.
How can they still see?

04:40.250 --> 04:41.250
Dr. Cherian,

04:41.791 --> 04:43.707
they don't need to see

04:43.708 --> 04:45.083
because they can hear.

04:47.291 --> 04:50.416
<i>Their hearing ability beats
that of an ordinary person.</i>

04:52.208 --> 04:54.499
Come in, Charlie One. It's a go!

04:54.500 --> 04:55.375
Go.

04:55.833 --> 04:56.750
One shot.

04:58.625 --> 04:59.541
One kill.

05:02.541 --> 05:03.458
No luck.

05:06.333 --> 05:07.250
All skill.

05:17.708 --> 05:18.583
Bomb defused.

05:19.708 --> 05:20.957
Hostages released, sir.

05:20.958 --> 05:22.333
Move! To the exit!

05:22.541 --> 05:24.708
<i>Team terrorists, you lost!
Get up!</i>

05:26.583 --> 05:27.749
<i>Chin up, guys. Chin up!</i>

05:27.750 --> 05:29.375
<i>- Great job, guys.
- Well done, boys.</i>

05:33.375 --> 05:35.500
That was a war games exercise!

05:35.916 --> 05:39.165
Ladies and gentlemen,
presenting Team Alpha.

05:39.166 --> 05:41.333
The first. The fastest.

05:41.708 --> 05:42.666
The strongest.

05:43.708 --> 05:45.666
<i>Reflexes matching an eagle.</i>

05:47.541 --> 05:49.583
<i>Strength to floor wrestlers.</i>

05:51.083 --> 05:54.083
<i>They've run in
minus 30-degree temperatures,</i>

05:54.750 --> 05:56.249
<i>where most people struggle to breathe.</i>

05:56.250 --> 05:59.040
<i>India's most elite and advanced
commando program.</i>

05:59.041 --> 06:02.832
Human lethal weapons, with Alpha
running through their veins.

06:02.833 --> 06:05.416
- Alpha?
- Yes, Alpha.

06:06.291 --> 06:08.625
The team was injected with the serum,

06:09.333 --> 06:11.416
then they were trained by our very best.

06:11.791 --> 06:13.958
Lt. Col. Vikrant Kaul.

06:15.375 --> 06:16.458
My Guru <i>ji.</i>

06:19.041 --> 06:21.000
I lost an eye in the Kargil attack,

06:21.708 --> 06:24.625
but my vision is sharper than ever.

06:24.958 --> 06:27.458
I trained Cobra, Ghatak
and many other teams,

06:27.708 --> 06:31.791
but I've never seen an attack team
like Alpha.

06:32.208 --> 06:33.375
They're bloody good.

06:34.000 --> 06:35.291
And that's an understatement.

06:36.833 --> 06:41.041
But according to protocol,
you should've taken clearance from DRDO.

06:42.750 --> 06:44.833
Do you know the meaning
of top secret, madam?

06:48.125 --> 06:49.832
"Strictly need-to-know basis."

06:49.833 --> 06:52.124
Understand what science means,
Col. Lakhawat?

06:52.125 --> 06:53.832
Or do you ignore it, too?

06:53.833 --> 06:55.708
You're the one who ignored it, madam.

06:56.291 --> 06:58.083
You didn't look carefully.

06:59.458 --> 07:02.875
The Chief Scientist in this program
is your senior

07:03.083 --> 07:05.000
in experience and qualification.

07:06.166 --> 07:07.541
Doctor John Verghese.

07:09.291 --> 07:10.250
Hello, everyone.

07:15.833 --> 07:16.791
The Alpha serum.

07:17.750 --> 07:22.208
It makes our tissues, muscles, and organs
stronger and more efficient.

07:22.500 --> 07:26.833
It improves vision, hearing,
reflexes, senses, and lungs.

07:27.750 --> 07:29.708
Improves everything.

07:31.041 --> 07:33.541
What if a soldier is hit by a bullet?

07:35.041 --> 07:37.666
Soldiers are not invincible.
They're human.

07:38.375 --> 07:41.749
A headshot would kill them.

07:41.750 --> 07:45.666
But if the wound isn't serious,
the Alpha serum can heal it.

07:46.791 --> 07:51.583
In nature, many creatures like lizards
and lobsters can regenerate.

07:52.208 --> 07:56.583
The Alpha serum acts on damaged organs
by mimicking that process.

07:57.208 --> 08:00.125
The initial idea was to facilitate…

08:01.583 --> 08:03.500
faster recovery for our soldiers.

08:04.000 --> 08:08.000
How often must this serum be administered?
Before every mission?

08:08.250 --> 08:09.500
Once you go Alpha,

08:10.291 --> 08:11.541
you can't go back.

08:13.000 --> 08:16.916
We need everyone's approval to
take this program to the next level.

08:32.458 --> 08:34.458
Did you talk to Janaki's sister?

08:34.708 --> 08:37.083
She was going to get a second opinion
in Spain.

08:37.708 --> 08:39.250
Yes, I received Aruna's email.

08:39.458 --> 08:40.916
I'm glad we found out in time.

08:41.041 --> 08:42.000
Found out what?

08:42.958 --> 08:46.375
I'm a bloody scientist, Preeti.
I don't believe in luck.

08:46.791 --> 08:49.416
Not in sugar-coating either.
Just give me the facts, please.

08:50.000 --> 08:50.958
It's confirmed.

08:52.500 --> 08:53.916
Congenital heart disease.

08:57.291 --> 09:00.000
During pregnancy, the mother's heart
has to work double.

09:01.291 --> 09:03.166
Your heart can't handle it.

09:04.291 --> 09:06.166
This is suicidal, Janaki.

09:06.375 --> 09:08.708
It's your first trimester.
It's still possible.

09:09.458 --> 09:10.500
You need to have an abortion.

09:12.750 --> 09:14.833
So I can never be a mother?

09:26.583 --> 09:28.166
We don't have a choice, Janaki.

09:29.375 --> 09:30.250
Please.

09:31.750 --> 09:32.958
I'm with you.

09:33.583 --> 09:34.958
We'll face it together.

09:35.333 --> 09:37.000
We've tried for so many years.

09:37.750 --> 09:39.041
It's too much of a risk.

09:39.666 --> 09:42.041
If I feared death,
I would not have married a soldier.

09:43.000 --> 09:46.333
I listened to my heart then,
and I'll listen to it now.

09:49.083 --> 09:50.041
My heart is weak,

09:53.041 --> 09:54.541
but it has made a decision.

09:55.000 --> 09:56.333
Why are you so stubborn?

09:58.625 --> 10:00.875
Stubborn girls change the world, Vikrant.

10:02.833 --> 10:04.958
This child has chosen us.

10:07.708 --> 10:09.208
We're having this baby.

10:10.666 --> 10:11.583
Promise me?

10:20.041 --> 10:21.833
<i>Your heart can't handle it.</i>

10:22.583 --> 10:26.249
<i>My heart is weak,
but it has made a decision.</i>

10:26.250 --> 10:30.583
<i>It makes our tissues, muscles, and organs
stronger and more efficient.</i>

10:31.916 --> 10:34.708
<i>The Alpha serum repairs
damaged organs.</i>

10:37.166 --> 10:38.625
<i>We're having this baby.</i>

10:41.833 --> 10:42.833
<i>Promise me?</i>

10:50.125 --> 10:51.458
This is a medical miracle.

10:52.208 --> 10:53.750
Janaki's heart is improving.

10:53.958 --> 10:57.083
It's showing rapid improvement.
And no complications with the pregnancy.

10:58.208 --> 11:00.208
Janaki, it's the last two months.

11:00.416 --> 11:01.375
So take care, okay?

11:02.833 --> 11:03.750
Thank you.

11:09.375 --> 11:10.291
Come.

11:19.416 --> 11:20.958
Our Alpha soldiers.

11:24.333 --> 11:25.291
Brain hemorrhage.

11:26.583 --> 11:29.291
Three of the six died on the spot
from a brain bleed.

11:30.666 --> 11:32.291
The other three are in the ICU.

11:33.375 --> 11:35.958
According to the program,
my team has been

11:36.708 --> 11:39.708
monitoring their vitals for the past
ten months. Every day.

11:41.125 --> 11:44.125
Their vitals were perfect.
There was no warning.

11:45.041 --> 11:47.958
- Sir, you know why this happened, right?
- Alpha.

11:57.833 --> 11:58.750
Move!

12:22.833 --> 12:24.833
<i>We're trying to save the child.</i>

12:29.458 --> 12:30.500
Guru <i>ji.</i>

12:30.833 --> 12:33.166
Did you give the Alpha serum to Janaki?

12:39.041 --> 12:42.582
I thought I would save her.

12:42.583 --> 12:45.916
You didn't save her. You killed her!

12:48.791 --> 12:51.625
Alpha is the property
of the Indian Government.

12:52.291 --> 12:56.125
It was only tried on soldiers,
who signed up for it.

12:56.500 --> 12:57.875
Do you understand what this means?

13:01.041 --> 13:04.791
The Alpha serum is running
through your child's veins.

13:05.875 --> 13:08.041
Your baby belongs to the country.

13:08.500 --> 13:11.291
Only the country has rights
over the child, not you.

13:16.541 --> 13:17.416
Vikrant.

13:20.291 --> 13:21.166
I'm sorry.

13:21.666 --> 13:23.166
We couldn't save Janaki.

13:36.250 --> 13:37.291
Take the baby away.

13:50.250 --> 13:51.208
Vikrant!

13:52.458 --> 13:53.625
Vikrant! Listen to me.

13:55.375 --> 13:56.791
They've taken your daughter.

14:07.291 --> 14:08.250
Where's my daughter?

14:15.500 --> 14:16.541
She's gone numb.

14:17.125 --> 14:18.208
She's cold.

14:20.333 --> 14:21.791
She's not breathing, Fateh.

14:22.208 --> 14:23.333
She's dead, Guru <i>ji.</i>

14:29.416 --> 14:30.916
You shouldn't have stolen the serum.

14:32.000 --> 14:33.625
But I won't let them arrest you.

14:34.208 --> 14:36.416
I respect soldiers like you.

14:40.666 --> 14:41.625
I was a soldier.

14:44.083 --> 14:44.958
I'm done.

15:03.750 --> 15:05.958
Internal Inquiry has testified that

15:06.166 --> 15:09.957
Alpha should have been tested
for another six months.

15:09.958 --> 15:11.125
But you pushed it.

15:11.583 --> 15:12.791
I did.

15:13.833 --> 15:16.625
Nor did I ask for anyone's permission.

15:16.916 --> 15:18.583
Six cadets are dead.

15:18.916 --> 15:21.000
If this version of Alpha had worked,

15:21.875 --> 15:23.666
how many cadets would've been saved?

15:24.375 --> 15:28.375
What use is blood
if it does not spill for the nation?

15:28.916 --> 15:32.708
A bullet didn't kill them.
Your negligence did.

15:33.041 --> 15:36.040
Disobeying orders is not a mistake.
It's a crime.

15:36.041 --> 15:39.540
Under normal circumstances,
the punishment is court-martial.

15:39.541 --> 15:42.624
But considering your exemplary
career record,

15:42.625 --> 15:46.208
this Committee has decided to take
disciplinary action instead.

15:46.666 --> 15:47.666
We're demoting you.

15:48.625 --> 15:51.333
<i>You'll be demoted from Colonel
to Lt. Colonel.</i>

15:53.333 --> 15:57.166
<i>You're now posted to the Cherrapunji
Special Forces base.</i>

15:58.958 --> 16:02.208
<i>A place where you'll never see
the battlefield again.</i>

16:08.708 --> 16:10.083
And as for the Alpha program,

16:10.791 --> 16:13.041
it has been shut down permanently.

16:17.083 --> 16:18.916
Despite this humiliation

16:19.875 --> 16:21.833
and this injustice,

16:23.458 --> 16:24.958
one thing has not changed.

16:26.333 --> 16:27.875
That I am a patriot.

16:29.166 --> 16:30.666
A true patriot.

16:32.666 --> 16:34.083
Mark my words.

16:35.291 --> 16:36.875
The day will come

16:38.875 --> 16:41.791
when you'll hold up my patriotism
as an example to the world.

16:45.041 --> 16:46.791
You have no idea that

16:48.125 --> 16:51.500
by shutting down Alpha today,

16:52.708 --> 16:55.333
what a grave mistake you've made.

16:58.250 --> 16:59.250
Not a mistake.

17:01.166 --> 17:02.125
A sin.

17:07.166 --> 17:08.166
<i>Jai Hind!</i>

17:35.250 --> 17:37.083
I need money and men.

17:37.833 --> 17:38.791
When can we meet?

18:09.875 --> 18:11.625
<i>Sir, I'm in Rajasthan,</i>

18:12.333 --> 18:14.416
and you're far away in Cherrapunji.

18:15.083 --> 18:17.083
How can we work together?

18:17.416 --> 18:21.500
I've been posted to such
an inconsequential place

18:22.333 --> 18:24.250
where no one watches me.

18:24.750 --> 18:26.333
Even though I'm posted in Cherrapunji,

18:26.916 --> 18:28.750
my full focus will be on our program.

18:30.750 --> 18:33.750
Look! Alpha's new facility.

18:34.291 --> 18:36.166
But how?

18:37.000 --> 18:38.041
There are some people

18:39.250 --> 18:41.666
who understand the importance of Alpha.

18:42.250 --> 18:43.208
Who are they, sir?

18:43.708 --> 18:45.916
A few patriots like me.

18:46.375 --> 18:47.708
This was their factory.

18:48.416 --> 18:49.875
Put all your focus on Alpha.

18:51.291 --> 18:52.708
Create a version of the serum

18:53.416 --> 18:56.375
that can be given to every Indian soldier.

18:57.000 --> 18:58.833
Sir, you never give up, do you?

19:00.000 --> 19:01.000
Why would I?

19:01.458 --> 19:04.583
Especially now that
I hold the ace in the pack.

19:12.750 --> 19:15.207
Sir, giving Col. Kaul a stillborn baby
that belonged to someone else

19:15.208 --> 19:18.166
and telling him it was his daughter
was wrong.

19:18.833 --> 19:21.958
Sometimes the line between
right and wrong is blurred, Verghese.

19:22.708 --> 19:26.041
And for me,
nothing matters more than Alpha.

19:30.916 --> 19:32.416
What should we call her, sir?

19:33.000 --> 19:35.041
Her mother's name was Janaki.

19:37.083 --> 19:38.208
We'll call her…

19:40.500 --> 19:41.875
Sita.

20:03.375 --> 20:06.874
The baby elephant is with his family,
who protects him.

20:06.875 --> 20:08.166
And my parents?

20:09.666 --> 20:10.583
Where are they?

20:11.958 --> 20:13.166
They abandoned you.

20:14.416 --> 20:15.916
Fateh sir brought you here.

20:28.916 --> 20:29.958
Verghese Uncle!

20:31.250 --> 20:33.458
<i>Verghese, is the effect
of Alpha showing?</i>

20:34.166 --> 20:35.250
<i>Not yet, sir.</i>

20:50.083 --> 20:51.708
Happy 12th birthday, Sita!

20:51.958 --> 20:53.583
Uncle, didn't Fateh sir come?

20:54.166 --> 20:56.958
He's very busy.
Otherwise, he'd be here.

20:58.208 --> 20:59.708
Wait. One minute.

21:01.875 --> 21:03.416
This is your birthday gift.

21:04.416 --> 21:05.291
Wow!

21:06.958 --> 21:07.875
Soldier!

21:20.375 --> 21:22.666
<i>Coding and hacking.
She's excellent at both, sir.</i>

21:23.708 --> 21:25.541
Way beyond her age.

21:26.166 --> 21:27.707
Her IQ is very high, sir.

21:27.708 --> 21:29.291
We don't need her to write a book.

21:30.333 --> 21:32.333
Tell me, has Alpha shown its effect?

22:07.875 --> 22:09.500
<i>It's the puberty hormone.</i>

22:10.125 --> 22:11.625
Alpha has finally kicked in.

22:12.416 --> 22:14.958
Through Sita, we'll be able
to develop a new version of Alpha.

22:29.833 --> 22:31.750
Are you crying? I see tears.

22:32.208 --> 22:33.125
Don't cry.

22:33.666 --> 22:37.916
People are either strong or weak.
Gender has nothing to do with it.

22:39.416 --> 22:41.958
<i>There are two kinds of people
in this world.</i>

22:42.250 --> 22:43.958
<i>Wolves and sheep.</i>

22:44.416 --> 22:45.375
I'm a wolf.

22:46.875 --> 22:47.750
What are you?

22:47.875 --> 22:49.416
A wolf's child is a wolf, sir.

22:55.291 --> 22:56.208
<i>Well done!</i>

22:56.666 --> 22:57.666
Here's your reward.

23:00.208 --> 23:02.332
What did you call your father?

23:02.333 --> 23:03.208
Baba.

23:04.291 --> 23:05.166
Baba.

23:08.000 --> 23:09.916
I got it for my first mission.

23:10.583 --> 23:12.458
When will I get my first mission?

23:13.416 --> 23:15.458
When you become an Indian soldier.

23:21.625 --> 23:22.666
What's this?

23:23.833 --> 23:24.708
Alpha.

23:25.666 --> 23:26.708
What's Alpha?

23:26.958 --> 23:29.125
The first letter of the Greek alphabet,

23:29.583 --> 23:31.291
and our program's motto.

23:32.166 --> 23:33.333
The first.

23:33.500 --> 23:34.791
The fastest.

23:35.208 --> 23:36.333
The strongest.

23:37.833 --> 23:40.291
If you look closely, every city
is an urban jungle,

23:41.125 --> 23:43.874
and in that jungle, Alpha rules.

23:43.875 --> 23:48.458
That's why I called the serum "Alpha."
And that's what you are.

23:49.375 --> 23:50.250
Alpha.

24:20.333 --> 24:21.332
Sir!

24:21.333 --> 24:24.082
Sir, it's Tel Aviv. The Mossad Chief
wants a word.

24:24.083 --> 24:26.915
- Cancel everything. This takes priority.
- Yes, sir.

24:26.916 --> 24:27.791
Let's get to it.

24:28.083 --> 24:29.332
- Karan.
- Yes, sir.

24:29.333 --> 24:30.666
- Show me.
- Sir.

24:32.208 --> 24:33.416
Sir, five bodies were found.

24:33.833 --> 24:35.666
The first was Subrato Das.

24:36.291 --> 24:37.666
<i>He was traveling alone
in the last metro.</i>

24:40.416 --> 24:42.083
<i>Just one stab. Dead.</i>

24:43.416 --> 24:45.458
<i>Five hours later, Amit Thakur.</i>

24:46.250 --> 24:48.166
<i>He saw someone ahead,
so he honked.</i>

24:49.958 --> 24:50.958
<i>The car was rigged.</i>

24:52.000 --> 24:54.875
Number three, Ajinkya Sethi.
A sniper kill, sir.

24:55.166 --> 24:58.750
The bullet went through the window and
his glasses, straight into his left eye.

25:00.791 --> 25:02.166
Next was Madhur Kulkarni.

25:03.458 --> 25:04.666
<i>In broad daylight, a headshot.</i>

25:05.708 --> 25:06.708
<i>Fearless.</i>

25:09.166 --> 25:12.625
The last and most ruthless, Susan Cherian.

25:18.500 --> 25:19.833
<i>Suffocated to death.</i>

25:22.625 --> 25:24.791
Sir, they've all been murdered
in the past 48 hours.

25:25.041 --> 25:27.333
All from different departments
and ministries.

25:27.583 --> 25:29.499
DRDO, NSA, NSG,

25:29.500 --> 25:31.915
Military Intelligence,
and the Ministry of Defense.

25:31.916 --> 25:36.000
We're trying to work out the common link
that made them targets.

25:44.666 --> 25:45.583
Alpha.

25:58.625 --> 26:01.541
ID Sita. 14:25 hours.

26:02.291 --> 26:03.250
Access granted.

26:31.875 --> 26:32.916
Where were you for the last two days?

26:35.500 --> 26:36.500
What are you eating?

26:39.875 --> 26:40.791
Thanks.

26:41.541 --> 26:42.500
I haven't had breakfast.

26:46.833 --> 26:47.750
So…

27:09.958 --> 27:11.583
Sita, what are you doing?

27:28.625 --> 27:29.666
Good morning, Baba.

27:31.250 --> 27:33.875
Today Sita herself has come
to burn Lanka.

27:47.583 --> 27:48.707
<i>Sita has gone crazy!</i>

27:48.708 --> 27:50.708
<i>She's killing everyone. Find her.</i>

27:54.666 --> 27:56.916
<i>Let's get her! Get the bombs!
Get the guns!</i>

28:09.750 --> 28:10.708
Grenade!

28:33.166 --> 28:34.041
Hi, boys.

29:30.375 --> 29:32.166
<i>Where are my parents?</i>

29:39.333 --> 29:40.874
<i>Happy 12th birthday, Sita!</i>

29:40.875 --> 29:42.583
<i>- Uncle, didn't Fateh sir come?
- He's very busy.</i>

29:44.333 --> 29:46.083
<i>I'm a wolf. What are you?</i>

29:46.416 --> 29:47.416
<i>One shot.</i>

29:47.875 --> 29:48.750
<i>One kill!</i>

29:49.500 --> 29:52.291
<i>There's only one punishment
for a traitor.</i>

29:52.541 --> 29:54.083
<i>On your 18th birthday,</i>

29:54.250 --> 29:56.291
<i>what could be more special than that?</i>

29:57.041 --> 29:58.041
<i>One kill!</i>

31:54.625 --> 31:56.583
<i>Target in sight! Target in sight!</i>

31:56.708 --> 31:57.875
<i>Sita is on the bridge.</i>

31:58.000 --> 32:01.041
<i>Don't lose visual. I repeat.
Do not lose the visual.</i>

32:01.541 --> 32:02.708
<i>No one will shoot!</i>

32:05.375 --> 32:06.625
Have you lost it?

32:07.041 --> 32:08.083
Hands up, Sita!

32:08.625 --> 32:09.791
Drop the gun!

32:11.333 --> 32:12.375
Put the gun down!

34:23.208 --> 34:28.541
Why did R&AW Chief Vikrant Kaul travel
to a remote corner of the country

34:28.875 --> 34:30.541
to meet a forgotten soldier?

34:35.000 --> 34:36.083
I had no choice.

34:37.833 --> 34:42.041
Honestly, Guru <i>ji,</i> stay out of this.
It's in your best interest.

34:42.458 --> 34:43.583
What are you up to, Fateh?

35:06.875 --> 35:07.875
<i>I've killed six.</i>

35:08.750 --> 35:09.666
<i>Now just two left.</i>

35:16.958 --> 35:17.875
Who is she?

35:18.208 --> 35:19.166
How did you get this?

35:22.291 --> 35:25.833
Look carefully. You know her.

35:26.166 --> 35:27.750
She's very close to you.

35:39.833 --> 35:41.916
I buried my daughter
with my own two hands.

35:43.125 --> 35:44.125
Sita.

35:45.708 --> 35:47.208
Her name is Sita.

35:58.000 --> 36:00.875
Sita became the Alpha soldier
we all hoped for.

36:01.500 --> 36:04.291
She was my pride. Our very best.

36:04.958 --> 36:06.583
Then one day she flipped.

36:07.041 --> 36:08.875
The serum twisted her brain.

36:09.458 --> 36:11.416
Everyone associated with the program…

36:12.541 --> 36:13.916
she's killing them all.

36:14.541 --> 36:17.500
Special Forces shut Alpha down
twenty years ago.

36:18.541 --> 36:19.791
How are you running it?

36:20.708 --> 36:22.875
Who is funding it?

36:25.625 --> 36:27.333
I never thought you'd become a traitor!

36:27.833 --> 36:29.791
Sita is the traitor, Guru <i>ji.</i>

36:30.208 --> 36:32.207
She's killing our national assets.

36:32.208 --> 36:35.541
Now she's after the R&AW Chief
and a Lt. Colonel.

36:36.208 --> 36:37.375
Don't worry.

36:37.666 --> 36:39.041
My men are looking for her.

36:39.458 --> 36:41.832
When they find her, they'll kill her.

36:41.833 --> 36:43.041
She's my daughter, Fateh.

36:43.416 --> 36:46.291
How? You don't even know her.

36:47.041 --> 36:51.375
You can't imagine how hard
it is for me to kill her.

36:52.583 --> 36:55.041
Your daughter died twenty years ago.

36:55.791 --> 36:57.333
Now she's my Sita.

36:59.708 --> 37:01.791
I'll expose the truth
about you to everyone,

37:02.458 --> 37:03.833
and you'll hang for it.

37:05.708 --> 37:06.666
I will.

37:09.166 --> 37:10.625
But only after Sita.

37:11.625 --> 37:14.041
After all, she's the one murdering people.

37:14.708 --> 37:17.708
Don't let your emotions cloud
your judgment again, Guru <i>ji.</i>

37:18.791 --> 37:20.583
The last time you did that,

37:21.666 --> 37:23.000
you lost your wife.

37:24.166 --> 37:25.833
This time it may be your daughter.

37:55.791 --> 37:56.833
I hate coffee.

37:58.166 --> 38:00.041
Baba gave me the habit, Soldier.

38:00.375 --> 38:02.041
One cup for him,

38:03.125 --> 38:04.041
and one for me.

38:05.041 --> 38:06.708
I'll have my last cup with him.

38:10.583 --> 38:12.250
I'll get our revenge, Soldier.

38:13.208 --> 38:14.750
Two lab rats have survived.

38:15.083 --> 38:16.791
But we'll kill Baba at the very end.

38:17.416 --> 38:19.000
Like enjoying a fine dessert
after lunch.

38:23.041 --> 38:24.500
We'll save the best for the last.

38:26.625 --> 38:29.291
But before that… Vikrant Kaul.

38:31.750 --> 38:34.000
Kaul. A Kashmiri Pandit surname.

38:34.208 --> 38:36.250
Sanskrit for "family."

38:37.625 --> 38:40.499
He left the army 20 years ago.
Then he went totally off the grid.

38:40.500 --> 38:43.875
After Luthra died, he was
suddenly appointed R&AW Chief.

38:44.291 --> 38:46.208
Congratulations, Vikrant!

38:51.666 --> 38:52.583
I love it.

39:01.083 --> 39:02.125
Okay.

39:02.583 --> 39:06.250
Two weeks ago, he flew from Delhi
to Madrid, from there to Valladolid.

39:06.791 --> 39:09.790
Four days later, he came back to India
from Spain.

39:09.791 --> 39:14.208
The same route last month.
In March too. And in December.

39:15.708 --> 39:17.416
These R&AW guys love travelling!

39:18.166 --> 39:19.416
He's in Spain again?

39:20.875 --> 39:21.791
Sad.

39:23.166 --> 39:25.166
We'll have to wait
till he's back in India.

39:33.250 --> 39:35.666
Soldier, all his trips to Spain
were on commercial flights.

39:36.791 --> 39:38.125
That means personal trips.

39:41.750 --> 39:43.625
What's special about Spain, Kaul?

40:11.416 --> 40:13.333
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

40:14.083 --> 40:16.166
<i>A firecracker</i>

40:16.500 --> 40:17.625
<i>No touching</i>

40:18.625 --> 40:20.957
<i>Lightning striking</i>

40:20.958 --> 40:22.333
<i>Girl's a storm</i>

40:23.333 --> 40:25.333
<i>Challenge her</i>

40:25.666 --> 40:26.958
<i>You've had it</i>

40:27.791 --> 40:29.875
<i>Acts first</i>

40:30.125 --> 40:31.458
<i>Thinks later</i>

40:32.750 --> 40:34.833
<i>Kohl-lined eyes</i>

40:35.000 --> 40:37.083
<i>Burning through the heart</i>

40:37.291 --> 40:40.541
<i>Encircles the heart
Now she's gone</i>

40:40.791 --> 40:43.040
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

40:43.041 --> 40:45.332
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

40:45.333 --> 40:47.791
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

40:47.916 --> 40:49.957
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

40:49.958 --> 40:52.124
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

40:52.125 --> 40:54.333
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

40:54.500 --> 40:56.915
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

40:56.916 --> 40:58.958
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

40:59.916 --> 41:01.958
<i>Soft breeze</i>

41:02.166 --> 41:04.375
<i>Wind perplexed</i>

41:04.500 --> 41:06.500
<i>Sturdy form</i>

41:06.750 --> 41:07.875
<i>Kickass</i>

41:08.000 --> 41:09.082
<i>Kickass</i>

41:09.083 --> 41:11.041
<i>Challenge her</i>

41:11.333 --> 41:13.541
<i>You've had it</i>

41:13.666 --> 41:15.541
<i>Acts first</i>

41:16.000 --> 41:17.041
<i>Thinks later</i>

41:40.625 --> 41:42.832
<i>Those eyes of hers</i>

41:42.833 --> 41:45.208
<i>Robs the whole village</i>

41:45.416 --> 41:47.665
<i>She heeds no one</i>

41:47.666 --> 41:49.457
<i>Her law is law</i>

41:49.458 --> 41:51.665
<i>Sweet as honey</i>

41:51.666 --> 41:53.915
<i>Melting in the mouth</i>

41:53.916 --> 41:56.832
<i>Showers colors</i>

41:56.833 --> 41:58.624
<i>To the world</i>

41:58.625 --> 42:00.665
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

42:00.666 --> 42:02.999
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

42:03.000 --> 42:05.665
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

42:05.666 --> 42:07.749
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

42:07.750 --> 42:09.832
<i>Girl's chilled Champagne</i>

42:09.833 --> 42:12.082
<i>Toned and maintained</i>

42:12.083 --> 42:14.541
<i>Cast off the evil eye</i>

42:14.750 --> 42:16.833
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

42:17.583 --> 42:19.541
<i>A firecracker</i>

42:19.875 --> 42:21.208
<i>No touching</i>

42:22.208 --> 42:24.125
<i>Lightning striking</i>

42:24.500 --> 42:25.708
<i>Girl's a storm</i>

42:26.916 --> 42:28.750
<i>Challenge her</i>

42:29.041 --> 42:30.333
<i>You've had it</i>

42:30.500 --> 42:33.290
<i>- Cast off the evil eye
- Acts first</i>

42:33.291 --> 42:35.000
<i>Girl's got style!</i>

43:06.041 --> 43:07.041
<i>Vikrant, listen to me.</i>

43:08.750 --> 43:10.208
They've taken your daughter.

43:10.875 --> 43:13.041
No, listen! I want to show you something.

43:13.375 --> 43:14.916
Just come. Just come with me.

43:15.333 --> 43:17.166
I overheard Colonel Fateh.

43:17.416 --> 43:21.041
The Alpha serum is running
through your child's veins.

43:21.625 --> 43:23.708
Your baby belongs to the country.

43:25.083 --> 43:26.208
Your other daughter.

43:28.375 --> 43:30.583
- What?
- I'm sorry, Vikrant.

43:30.833 --> 43:34.333
Janaki knew, but she didn't tell you.
She also stopped me from telling you.

43:36.041 --> 43:37.458
Having one baby was a risk,

43:38.208 --> 43:41.291
and she knew you'd never let her
carry two babies.

43:42.541 --> 43:45.166
They're twins, but not identical.

43:46.041 --> 43:48.333
The sister, who was born first,
protected the other.

43:49.916 --> 43:53.415
No one must know about this.
And please--

43:53.416 --> 43:54.708
I'll delete all the records.

43:59.958 --> 44:02.458
<i>Thanks, Aruna, for bringing her here.</i>

44:02.875 --> 44:05.250
Vikrant, how will you live without her?

44:06.416 --> 44:07.708
She's our niece.

44:08.416 --> 44:09.958
We'll be more than happy
to have her, but…

44:10.625 --> 44:11.666
you're her father.

44:12.291 --> 44:14.208
I have no option, Manish.

44:14.916 --> 44:16.791
No one must know she's my daughter.

44:18.625 --> 44:20.250
I want her to lead a normal life.

44:20.416 --> 44:23.208
When she's older and starts
asking questions…

44:24.208 --> 44:25.250
I'll tell her the truth

44:27.458 --> 44:29.458
about what happened
to her mother and sister.

44:32.333 --> 44:33.916
Thought of a name for her?

44:34.500 --> 44:35.791
You know Janaki loved this name…

44:37.750 --> 44:38.708
Durga.

44:40.500 --> 44:43.666
The destroyer of demons. Durga.

44:45.500 --> 44:47.541
I always said you were special.

44:48.041 --> 44:49.541
There was no one like you.

44:50.583 --> 44:51.583
But there is someone, Durga.

44:52.458 --> 44:53.583
She's just like you.

44:57.833 --> 45:00.833
<i>This is Mom, this is you,
and this is my sister.</i>

45:01.041 --> 45:02.500
<i>And I'm the one behind her.</i>

45:02.958 --> 45:04.791
<i>She always protected me.</i>

45:05.375 --> 45:07.750
Pa, did you think of a name for her?

45:16.250 --> 45:17.291
Si…

45:18.791 --> 45:19.791
Sita?

45:22.166 --> 45:24.083
- Is she okay?
- She's in terrible danger.

45:27.000 --> 45:28.541
Fateh will kill her.

45:30.166 --> 45:31.208
Or she'll kill Fateh.

45:33.500 --> 45:34.500
And you too.

45:35.625 --> 45:37.708
To be honest, she should kill me.

45:38.000 --> 45:39.790
Because I've been
a horrible father to her.

45:39.791 --> 45:41.375
What? No, no, no.
Pa, listen to me.

45:42.000 --> 45:43.458
You're the best father in the world.

45:44.583 --> 45:46.791
When you got the chance,
you did your best.

45:48.041 --> 45:49.625
What happened was not your fault.

45:52.500 --> 45:53.583
I need your help.

45:55.958 --> 45:57.166
We need to find her.

45:57.791 --> 45:59.833
We have to save her at any cost.

46:02.291 --> 46:03.458
If Sita is caught,

46:04.583 --> 46:06.875
she'll be arrested for the murders.

46:07.500 --> 46:09.916
As the R&AW Chief,
I can't protect her officially.

46:11.291 --> 46:12.666
We have to do it unofficially.

46:13.541 --> 46:15.416
Only you and me.

46:16.041 --> 46:18.833
For Sita. For our family.

46:19.375 --> 46:21.416
Maybe I trained you for this day.

46:27.708 --> 46:33.000
Pa, not a day has gone by that
I haven't missed my sister, Sita.

46:34.833 --> 46:37.333
She was born first
so she could protect me.

46:38.333 --> 46:41.000
I've always wondered
how I'd ever repay her.

46:43.708 --> 46:45.250
I guess this is my only chance.

46:47.500 --> 46:49.000
Let's bring Sita home, Pa.

46:51.250 --> 46:53.041
Let's make our family a family again.

47:01.250 --> 47:02.291
We got him, Soldier!

47:05.291 --> 47:08.083
Yes! Mr. Family Man
is coming back to India.

47:08.458 --> 47:12.291
Spain Air 5837A. Madrid to Delhi,
Delhi to Srinagar.

47:13.000 --> 47:14.750
Srinagar? Kashmir?

47:15.458 --> 47:16.458
Why Kashmir?

47:23.958 --> 47:24.958
Come on, Sita!

47:25.833 --> 47:28.166
He's Kashmiri. Of course
he'd have a home in Kashmir.

47:28.625 --> 47:31.791
Vikrant Kaul,
property registrations? Nothing.

47:36.791 --> 47:37.915
<i>Any other family member?</i>

47:37.916 --> 47:39.458
<i>Janaki Kaul. Wife.</i>

47:43.791 --> 47:44.666
Boom!

47:48.541 --> 47:49.791
Nicely done, Janaki.

47:50.458 --> 47:52.083
Such a huge house in Betaab Valley!

48:16.083 --> 48:17.000
Cool.

48:37.541 --> 48:38.416
Pretty.

49:07.166 --> 49:08.500
Was it necessary to travel separately?

49:08.791 --> 49:10.666
<i>It's for your own safety, kiddo.</i>

49:10.958 --> 49:12.833
Being careful is the new brave.

49:13.958 --> 49:16.375
That's quite cool. Just like this house.

49:18.750 --> 49:21.750
Wow, Pa! Ma had some great taste.

49:21.875 --> 49:23.708
This is so beautiful!

49:24.166 --> 49:27.457
This place has been my off-grid
personal base for years.

49:27.458 --> 49:29.083
<i>It's my own safe house.</i>

49:29.541 --> 49:31.875
The kitchen is completely stocked up.

49:32.125 --> 49:34.083
Your favorite Italian coffee
is there too.

49:35.000 --> 49:35.875
Coffee.

49:36.041 --> 49:37.333
I'll get there ASAP.

49:37.458 --> 49:38.541
<i>Okay. See you, Pa.</i>

49:38.750 --> 49:39.958
- Love you.
- Love you.

50:19.333 --> 50:20.208
Cool.

51:46.000 --> 51:47.083
Sita?

51:48.208 --> 51:49.916
Fateh sent you for me?

51:53.000 --> 51:54.083
He has hurt my ego.

51:55.375 --> 51:57.708
No, no, no. I'm so sorry.
I didn't know.

51:57.916 --> 51:59.250
I'm your sister.

52:01.666 --> 52:02.583
Sister?

52:04.000 --> 52:04.958
Should I tie you a <i>rakhi?</i>

52:25.250 --> 52:26.208
Sita.

52:28.375 --> 52:31.208
I just want to talk to you. Please.

52:31.791 --> 52:32.791
The rule is simple.

52:33.333 --> 52:35.875
If you can stop me, then you get to talk.

52:46.916 --> 52:47.916
Can we talk now?

53:05.250 --> 53:06.250
Still wanna talk?

54:21.625 --> 54:22.958
So you wanna sit and talk?

54:24.208 --> 54:25.125
Okay.

54:27.583 --> 54:28.875
You shouldn't have laughed.

55:01.958 --> 55:04.708
Sita… that's our father.

55:23.041 --> 55:23.958
Sita.

55:25.875 --> 55:26.833
Papa.

55:36.583 --> 55:37.458
Pa!

55:46.875 --> 55:47.958
We don't look alike.

56:13.416 --> 56:14.291
Want some?

56:15.333 --> 56:16.625
You've gotten plenty of cardio too.

56:17.916 --> 56:18.791
Don't eat.

56:19.083 --> 56:20.875
I'm just loving this <i>desi</i> Chinese.

56:22.916 --> 56:23.791
I…

56:24.458 --> 56:25.708
I'm so sorry, kiddo.

56:29.208 --> 56:30.125
"Kiddo"?

56:32.125 --> 56:33.458
Don't get ahead of yourself, Kaul.

56:34.666 --> 56:35.583
And you?

56:35.875 --> 56:36.916
What nonsense were you saying?

56:38.166 --> 56:40.666
That we're sisters?
And he's our father?

56:41.166 --> 56:42.166
That's the truth.

56:42.416 --> 56:43.291
Shut up!

56:47.583 --> 56:48.458
Who is she?

56:50.291 --> 56:51.166
My mother?

56:51.541 --> 56:53.500
Yes. Janaki.

56:54.458 --> 56:56.416
- Didn't she come on the family vacation?
- She died…

56:57.250 --> 56:58.750
after giving birth to you both.

57:03.000 --> 57:03.875
Sita…

57:06.375 --> 57:09.208
you and I are twins.
I'm exactly like you.

57:11.208 --> 57:12.708
Look, sis, you're good.

57:13.125 --> 57:14.750
It's been a while since
anyone challenged me.

57:16.916 --> 57:18.333
But exactly like me?

57:27.875 --> 57:29.083
Who are these two boring people?

57:29.708 --> 57:30.625
My parents.

57:31.333 --> 57:32.875
I mean, my adoptive parents.

57:35.708 --> 57:38.000
Adoptive parents?

57:46.250 --> 57:47.666
How many parents does she have?

57:47.791 --> 57:48.708
Listen to me--

57:56.958 --> 58:00.083
She has three parents here
and one in heaven.

58:01.375 --> 58:02.541
And what did I get?

58:04.583 --> 58:05.458
Fateh.

58:07.958 --> 58:09.833
What's the difference between
a guinea pig and me?

58:13.083 --> 58:17.333
What is the difference between
a guinea pig and me, Kaul?

58:22.041 --> 58:25.124
After a few days of experiments,
the guinea pig

58:25.125 --> 58:27.541
is put down using sodium pentobarbital.

58:29.958 --> 58:32.541
And me? I didn't even get that option.

58:38.833 --> 58:41.291
Sita, Fateh lied to Pa.

58:41.916 --> 58:43.833
Pa thought you were dead all this time.

58:45.083 --> 58:46.416
If I'd known about you,

58:46.708 --> 58:49.790
none of this would've happened.
I'd have come to save you.

58:49.791 --> 58:50.750
Like you've come today?

59:01.083 --> 59:02.000
What is it, sis?

59:03.458 --> 59:04.541
Feeling bad for me?

59:16.208 --> 59:17.708
Honestly, I feel bad for you.

59:18.083 --> 59:19.166
What's this circus?

59:19.750 --> 59:20.750
What's going on here?

59:21.958 --> 59:22.915
Birthday.

59:22.916 --> 59:24.375
- Which one?
- Eighteenth.

59:28.000 --> 59:29.041
Eighteenth birthday?

59:31.250 --> 59:32.666
Same day, right?

59:35.833 --> 59:38.166
I wish I had a photo
from my 18th birthday.

59:39.000 --> 59:40.708
Quite the party it was!

59:44.958 --> 59:46.958
Happy 18th birthday, Sita.

59:47.333 --> 59:48.333
Thank you, Baba.

59:49.958 --> 59:53.625
Thank you for the dress
and for the dinner.

59:54.000 --> 59:55.125
Thank you for everything.

59:55.708 --> 59:56.958
It really means a lot to me.

01:00:13.916 --> 01:00:14.833
Wazeer.

01:00:15.083 --> 01:00:16.083
Arms dealer.

01:00:18.666 --> 01:00:20.791
He's a bloody traitor.

01:00:23.458 --> 01:00:24.541
Kill him.

01:00:25.250 --> 01:00:28.916
And then you'll see what
a soldier's life is all about.

01:00:32.791 --> 01:00:34.458
So all this wasn't for my birthday?

01:00:35.875 --> 01:00:37.500
On your 18th birthday,

01:00:37.750 --> 01:00:40.375
you're going to undertake your
first mission for the country.

01:00:41.500 --> 01:00:43.625
What could be more special than that?

01:01:16.000 --> 01:01:18.250
Take off your clothes and come.

01:01:18.625 --> 01:01:19.541
Join the party.

01:01:55.458 --> 01:01:56.416
Happy birthday!

01:02:02.208 --> 01:02:03.333
That was the first time.

01:02:05.416 --> 01:02:06.416
My first kill.

01:02:08.916 --> 01:02:12.333
After that, Fateh kept giving me targets,
and I kept killing them.

01:02:14.583 --> 01:02:17.916
Fateh got his Alpha soldier,
and I got my life's purpose.

01:02:20.750 --> 01:02:22.750
Then one day, everything changed.

01:02:25.875 --> 01:02:28.333
Next target. John Verghese.

01:02:33.875 --> 01:02:36.333
Stay sharp, or you're dead.

01:02:39.875 --> 01:02:42.666
Baba, how can I kill Dr. Verghese?

01:02:43.083 --> 01:02:44.291
Verghese is a traitor.

01:02:45.041 --> 01:02:46.958
He betrayed the country.

01:02:47.750 --> 01:02:50.291
And there's only one punishment
for a traitor.

01:03:01.958 --> 01:03:04.458
There's only one punishment for a traitor.

01:03:06.000 --> 01:03:06.957
Death.

01:03:06.958 --> 01:03:08.625
There's only one punishment for a traitor!

01:03:09.416 --> 01:03:10.291
Death.

01:03:15.666 --> 01:03:18.541
<i>For me, Baba's words were always
set in stone.</i>

01:03:19.416 --> 01:03:20.291
Yes.

01:03:28.416 --> 01:03:29.541
<i>But for the first time,</i>

01:03:30.291 --> 01:03:31.333
<i>I couldn't shoot.</i>

01:03:31.875 --> 01:03:33.541
I was waiting for you, Sita.

01:03:38.708 --> 01:03:40.750
Before dying,
I wanted to tell you something.

01:03:43.125 --> 01:03:47.458
And then Uncle Verghese told me
the story of my life.

01:03:50.500 --> 01:03:51.458
And Alpha's.

01:03:52.166 --> 01:03:53.666
<i>Have you ever thought about Alpha?</i>

01:03:54.583 --> 01:03:56.916
<i>Why aren't there more soldiers like you?</i>

01:03:59.166 --> 01:04:01.708
Because everyone who was given
the Alpha serum has died,

01:04:02.458 --> 01:04:03.500
except you.

01:04:06.208 --> 01:04:07.958
Fateh has only one purpose in life.

01:04:08.708 --> 01:04:11.916
To find out how more soldiers
like you could be created.

01:04:12.708 --> 01:04:15.916
You might remember that I collected
your blood samples every week

01:04:16.541 --> 01:04:19.541
to try and understand how you were
the only survivor.

01:04:19.791 --> 01:04:21.333
Why the serum hadn't killed you,

01:04:22.416 --> 01:04:25.708
and whether I could make a new version
of Alpha from your blood?

01:04:26.708 --> 01:04:29.041
But we didn't have cadets to test it on.

01:04:29.333 --> 01:04:32.583
So, Fateh had to find new subjects.

01:04:35.000 --> 01:04:40.000
Ordinary, innocent people
became the new test subjects…

01:04:42.375 --> 01:04:43.541
<i>but none of the poor souls survived.</i>

01:04:47.666 --> 01:04:49.541
Then we found this old graveyard.

01:04:52.666 --> 01:04:56.208
Fateh filled every grave here.

01:05:00.041 --> 01:05:05.208
And he's ready to fill one last grave…

01:05:07.833 --> 01:05:09.416
but I can't let that happen.

01:05:10.458 --> 01:05:11.458
What do you mean?

01:05:12.833 --> 01:05:18.000
The new version of Alpha
will not fail, Sita.

01:05:25.041 --> 01:05:26.125
What are you hiding?

01:05:28.416 --> 01:05:29.500
A few days ago,

01:05:29.791 --> 01:05:33.666
<i>Fateh found my research
on the new version of Alpha.</i>

01:05:33.916 --> 01:05:35.541
Verghese, you turned out to be weak.

01:05:36.500 --> 01:05:38.791
Spending time with Sita

01:05:39.625 --> 01:05:40.791
has made you emotional.

01:05:41.541 --> 01:05:43.541
How dare you hide this from me?

01:05:44.958 --> 01:05:46.333
We can't do this.

01:05:48.166 --> 01:05:51.250
We cannot harvest the serum
from Sita's brain cells.

01:05:53.125 --> 01:05:56.416
The poor girl will remain
in a medical coma for life.

01:06:02.583 --> 01:06:04.250
<i>She'll become a living corpse.</i>

01:06:05.208 --> 01:06:06.625
You can't do this, sir.

01:06:07.833 --> 01:06:10.125
Sita will be sentenced
to a living death, sir.

01:06:18.708 --> 01:06:19.625
Verghese…

01:06:21.458 --> 01:06:23.291
bravery demands sacrifice.

01:06:30.458 --> 01:06:31.458
Baba.

01:06:38.750 --> 01:06:39.750
Baba.

01:06:43.708 --> 01:06:45.583
Fateh is ready to kill me?

01:06:51.083 --> 01:06:54.166
He didn't just stop there.

01:06:54.875 --> 01:06:58.916
After he found the research,
a man came to meet him.

01:07:04.125 --> 01:07:05.375
The new version of Alpha.

01:07:08.916 --> 01:07:10.041
Congratulations!

01:07:14.125 --> 01:07:16.291
There's no stopping Operation Odyssey now.

01:07:21.458 --> 01:07:24.791
<i>I have no idea what Operation Odyssey is.</i>

01:07:25.583 --> 01:07:28.250
I was scared.
That's why I ran away from the lab.

01:07:28.500 --> 01:07:32.125
I tried to warn a few people
about Fateh's evil plans.

01:07:33.166 --> 01:07:35.791
They were the same people who approved

01:07:36.625 --> 01:07:38.750
the Alpha program twenty years ago.

01:07:57.333 --> 01:07:59.250
Fateh claimed they were all traitors.

01:07:59.916 --> 01:08:02.916
They weren't traitors.
The real traitor is Fateh.

01:08:03.833 --> 01:08:05.916
Fateh's mission must be stopped, Sita.

01:08:06.708 --> 01:08:08.041
He's a threat to you.

01:08:08.708 --> 01:08:11.208
The secret behind the Alpha serum
lies within you.

01:08:14.833 --> 01:08:15.791
So, my dear…

01:08:18.416 --> 01:08:19.416
run away.

01:08:20.250 --> 01:08:21.458
Far from the facility.

01:08:21.875 --> 01:08:25.083
A new team of doctors and surgeons
is coming for the procedure.

01:08:25.875 --> 01:08:27.000
- Don't go there.
- Let them come.

01:08:28.375 --> 01:08:33.833
This procedure, the new Alpha program,
can only exist if the facility exists.

01:08:35.416 --> 01:08:36.708
If Fateh exists.

01:08:46.666 --> 01:08:47.541
Sita.

01:08:49.916 --> 01:08:53.875
There's a man in that photo,
R&AW Chief Vikrant Kaul.

01:08:55.041 --> 01:08:55.958
Go meet him.

01:08:56.458 --> 01:08:57.958
He has a story to tell you.

01:09:00.375 --> 01:09:01.333
Uncle, no!

01:09:20.916 --> 01:09:22.750
Verghese Uncle wanted me to meet you.

01:09:24.000 --> 01:09:25.083
Now I know why.

01:09:26.416 --> 01:09:28.125
He believed we'd have
a happy family reunion.

01:09:30.583 --> 01:09:32.875
But we only have one thing in common.

01:09:34.333 --> 01:09:37.250
Our stupidity.
We fell straight into Fateh's trap.

01:09:37.666 --> 01:09:39.458
I came here to talk to you,
not to kill you.

01:09:40.750 --> 01:09:41.625
You guys are free to go.

01:09:46.000 --> 01:09:46.958
Where are you going?

01:09:48.750 --> 01:09:51.041
I'm going for Fateh.
Don't follow me.

01:09:51.166 --> 01:09:52.083
No.

01:09:53.541 --> 01:09:54.416
You're not.

01:09:55.458 --> 01:09:57.625
You two will stay here.
Safe and secure.

01:09:59.083 --> 01:10:01.000
I'll deal with him. Durga.

01:10:03.625 --> 01:10:04.666
Back off, Kaul.

01:10:05.916 --> 01:10:06.916
Don't play the father.

01:10:07.708 --> 01:10:10.041
I've tried the family scene with Fateh.

01:10:11.041 --> 01:10:12.041
It's not for me.

01:10:13.000 --> 01:10:16.416
Before I change my mind
and blow your brains out,

01:10:16.708 --> 01:10:17.583
go.

01:10:18.125 --> 01:10:19.375
I'm not going anywhere.

01:10:21.625 --> 01:10:23.291
I lost my daughter once.

01:10:26.041 --> 01:10:27.250
I can't lose her again.

01:10:33.083 --> 01:10:34.458
You already have a daughter, Kaul.

01:10:35.291 --> 01:10:36.666
You celebrate her birthdays,

01:10:37.166 --> 01:10:39.791
you celebrate every silly thing
about her life.

01:10:42.458 --> 01:10:43.666
I mean nothing to you.

01:10:44.500 --> 01:10:46.291
But if you're still finding it hard,

01:10:46.583 --> 01:10:48.666
just believe what you've believed
for all these years.

01:10:49.541 --> 01:10:52.916
That this daughter of yours
died at birth.

01:10:54.125 --> 01:10:55.041
Okay?

01:10:57.083 --> 01:10:57.958
Guys!

01:11:09.458 --> 01:11:11.958
Heavy boots. All around us.

01:11:16.541 --> 01:11:17.416
They're armed.

01:11:18.125 --> 01:11:19.083
Rifles.

01:11:24.791 --> 01:11:26.375
Fateh followed me.

01:12:01.708 --> 01:12:02.875
Found Sita?

01:12:03.291 --> 01:12:05.541
Yes, sir. A bike was found
outside the house.

01:12:06.166 --> 01:12:08.833
I confirm that both
Kaul and Sita are inside.

01:12:09.000 --> 01:12:10.833
Sita mustn't be harmed.

01:12:12.666 --> 01:12:14.166
I want her alive.

01:12:16.000 --> 01:12:17.000
And Kaul, sir?

01:12:17.416 --> 01:12:19.125
Find Sita, then kill him.

01:12:19.791 --> 01:12:20.708
<i>Copy that, sir.</i>

01:12:26.541 --> 01:12:28.333
Don't take Fateh lightly, Sita.

01:12:29.750 --> 01:12:31.375
He's the lion of his jungle.

01:12:34.125 --> 01:12:37.791
Lions only pretend to be ferocious.

01:12:39.750 --> 01:12:41.875
It's the lioness who goes for the kill.

01:12:43.875 --> 01:12:45.416
And don't forget, my name is Sita!

01:12:47.833 --> 01:12:49.583
Let the trial of fire begin!

01:13:21.583 --> 01:13:22.750
Sniper, take the shot!

01:13:47.333 --> 01:13:48.208
R&AW Chief.

01:13:54.208 --> 01:13:56.333
My armory. Come, let's move.

01:13:57.708 --> 01:13:59.915
<i>Tools out!
Cutters, pluckers, hammers!</i>

01:13:59.916 --> 01:14:01.583
<i>Come on! Break in!</i>

01:14:11.041 --> 01:14:11.958
<i>Move in! Move in!</i>

01:14:15.541 --> 01:14:16.625
Both of you, leave.

01:14:16.958 --> 01:14:19.708
There's a door that leads to the forest.

01:14:20.041 --> 01:14:21.208
Come on, girls. Now!

01:14:21.416 --> 01:14:23.166
I don't run away
from the battlefield, Kaul.

01:14:23.541 --> 01:14:26.833
This is not running.
It's called a strategic retreat.

01:14:27.208 --> 01:14:29.500
Sometimes stepping back
is moving forward in war.

01:14:29.750 --> 01:14:31.457
And right now, there's a whole army
out there.

01:14:31.458 --> 01:14:34.125
How many? Twenty? Thirty?

01:14:34.458 --> 01:14:35.915
- Listen…
- It's not your cup of tea…

01:14:35.916 --> 01:14:38.332
- Listen to me.
- but this is what Fateh trained me for.

01:14:38.333 --> 01:14:39.333
And I trained him!

01:14:42.041 --> 01:14:44.708
Sita, I know it's hard,

01:14:45.041 --> 01:14:47.625
but right now you have to trust Pa.

01:14:50.541 --> 01:14:51.500
How can I trust anyone?

01:14:52.625 --> 01:14:54.041
Put yourself in my shoes.

01:14:54.625 --> 01:14:56.333
That's what I've done since
I was a kid.

01:14:56.958 --> 01:14:58.708
When I found out you were still alive,

01:14:58.916 --> 01:15:01.333
I've often wondered what if it was…

01:15:03.291 --> 01:15:04.166
me.

01:15:04.875 --> 01:15:08.375
If I was born a few seconds
before you on that day,

01:15:08.916 --> 01:15:10.750
what would've happened?

01:15:13.750 --> 01:15:15.541
I would've been raised in a lab,

01:15:16.500 --> 01:15:18.916
and you would have had a normal life
in Spain.

01:15:20.208 --> 01:15:21.166
But, Sita,

01:15:22.333 --> 01:15:24.333
you protected me.

01:15:26.958 --> 01:15:30.708
Please give Pa a chance
to protect you today.

01:15:33.958 --> 01:15:35.041
<i>Prepare for entry.</i>

01:15:38.416 --> 01:15:41.208
We're running out of time.
Give me 72 hours.

01:15:41.416 --> 01:15:42.416
You want Fateh, right?

01:15:42.666 --> 01:15:44.541
I'll bring him to you.
I promise you that.

01:15:50.750 --> 01:15:51.625
Okay.

01:15:55.208 --> 01:15:56.333
This phone has the coordinates

01:15:57.208 --> 01:15:58.208
of a safe house.

01:15:58.750 --> 01:16:00.540
Avoid highways and check posts.

01:16:00.541 --> 01:16:02.250
Any more basic advice?

01:16:03.125 --> 01:16:05.375
Yes. The most basic of all.

01:16:06.625 --> 01:16:07.708
Take care of each other.

01:16:11.041 --> 01:16:12.041
Let's go.

01:16:20.333 --> 01:16:21.208
The door?

01:17:50.666 --> 01:17:53.291
Sir, Kaul is dead. We've found Sita.

01:17:53.958 --> 01:17:55.333
<i>Awaiting your instructions.</i>

01:17:56.875 --> 01:17:58.583
I'm coming to Kashmir to see Sita.

01:17:59.958 --> 01:18:01.750
I'll send you the location.
Bring her there.

01:18:07.916 --> 01:18:08.833
This is Kaul.

01:18:09.291 --> 01:18:11.458
I'll need a few more days before
returning to headquarters.

01:18:11.916 --> 01:18:13.208
I'm away on a personal matter.

01:18:14.333 --> 01:18:15.416
But I've found something.

01:18:16.750 --> 01:18:19.541
Only one word. Odyssey.

01:18:21.916 --> 01:18:24.583
Get me any intel you have on it
from the last 20 years.

01:18:26.125 --> 01:18:28.125
I want it in my inbox within four hours.

01:18:44.083 --> 01:18:45.583
Stop staring and sleep.

01:18:47.333 --> 01:18:49.249
You need at least six hours of sleep.

01:18:49.250 --> 01:18:51.874
Or else, your brain will start producing
excess cortisol.

01:18:51.875 --> 01:18:54.832
And then, you'll lose focus
and spoil my mood.

01:18:54.833 --> 01:18:56.416
No way! You have insomnia too?

01:18:58.166 --> 01:18:59.041
Too?

01:19:01.833 --> 01:19:04.833
Look, apart from Alpha, there's nothing
in common between us.

01:19:07.166 --> 01:19:09.125
Do you always put on this tough-girl act?

01:19:11.541 --> 01:19:13.208
You must feel some emotion.

01:19:13.625 --> 01:19:16.041
Like deep inside.

01:19:18.541 --> 01:19:21.665
If you only feel good when you're
killing someone,

01:19:21.666 --> 01:19:23.791
something deep inside you dies.

01:19:26.250 --> 01:19:28.416
This tough-girl act isn't an act.

01:19:30.083 --> 01:19:31.708
If you were with me,
you would have understood.

01:19:37.125 --> 01:19:38.750
I am with you now.

01:19:42.291 --> 01:19:44.083
You can trust me, you know.

01:19:46.291 --> 01:19:48.958
If I said I trusted you,

01:19:50.583 --> 01:19:52.124
would you let me sleep?

01:19:52.125 --> 01:19:53.708
Of course! I'll sing you a lullaby too!

01:19:55.333 --> 01:19:56.290
Should I?

01:19:56.291 --> 01:19:58.708
- Please keep an arm's distance.
- Okay. Easy.

01:19:58.875 --> 01:20:00.083
- Breathe in.
- Move back!

01:20:00.791 --> 01:20:01.750
Breathe out.

01:20:01.875 --> 01:20:04.625
<i>Do you mind takin' me
For a spin around, eh?</i>

01:20:04.916 --> 01:20:06.957
<i>Wanna check out if you're in the vibe, eh</i>

01:20:06.958 --> 01:20:09.083
<i>She be rollin' like a movie star bae</i>

01:20:09.208 --> 01:20:14.416
<i>- We in this together ride or die, eh
- Nothing to fear with you here</i>

01:20:14.666 --> 01:20:18.707
<i>With you by my side
I'll stop the storm</i>

01:20:18.708 --> 01:20:20.916
<i>Let me have my way</i>

01:20:21.083 --> 01:20:23.000
<i>Your way is good too</i>

01:20:23.291 --> 01:20:27.708
<i>Let us take a leap of faith</i>

01:20:31.333 --> 01:20:35.416
<i>O friend, now I've found you</i>

01:20:35.708 --> 01:20:39.666
<i>This world will dance on my fingertips</i>

01:20:39.958 --> 01:20:44.000
<i>O friend, for sure</i>

01:20:44.250 --> 01:20:48.290
<i>I'll make the sky fall to the ground</i>

01:20:48.291 --> 01:20:51.541
<i>Do you mind takin' me
For a spin around, eh?</i>

01:20:51.750 --> 01:20:53.708
<i>Wanna check out if you're in the vibe, eh</i>

01:20:53.916 --> 01:20:56.082
<i>She be rollin' like a movie star bae</i>

01:20:56.083 --> 01:20:57.415
<i>We in this together ride or die, eh</i>

01:20:57.416 --> 01:21:00.415
<i>Do you mind takin' me
For a spin around, eh?</i>

01:21:00.416 --> 01:21:02.582
<i>Wanna check out if you're in the vibe, eh</i>

01:21:02.583 --> 01:21:04.625
<i>She be rollin' like a movie star bae</i>

01:21:04.750 --> 01:21:06.708
<i>We in this together ride or die, eh</i>

01:21:24.125 --> 01:21:28.166
<i>Now that I've found you</i>

01:21:29.041 --> 01:21:32.750
<i>All sorrows are disappearing</i>

01:21:33.083 --> 01:21:37.083
<i>All the small joys of life</i>

01:21:37.666 --> 01:21:41.041
<i>All so clear to me now</i>

01:21:45.791 --> 01:21:48.750
<i>There's nothing we can't do</i>

01:21:49.208 --> 01:21:54.125
<i>Things that no one could imagine</i>

01:21:54.416 --> 01:21:57.500
<i>We overcame the challenges through love</i>

01:21:57.833 --> 01:22:02.207
<i>No one can stop us now</i>

01:22:02.208 --> 01:22:06.290
<i>The world can work wonders
And so can we</i>

01:22:06.291 --> 01:22:10.665
<i>With you by my side
We'll make the river part</i>

01:22:10.666 --> 01:22:14.833
<i>Nothing to fear with you here</i>

01:22:14.958 --> 01:22:18.833
<i>With you by my side
I'll stop the storm</i>

